From: AsherJN
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Do not close the msync alert index on thread exit.

Adapted for CrossOver 26.3 from AsherJN/recall commit a436e4cd4fac44693b4d699acc030d17eec6f36e
(patches/wine-ntdll-syscall-log.patch, the pthread_exit_wrapper hunk only;
its diagnostics are not carried). A downstream fix, not a WineHQ backport.

Under msync, a thread's in-process alert "fd" is the index of its alert
object in the server's shared object table, not a file descriptor, yet
thread exit still close()d it. That closed whatever the process had open
under that number: a file, a pipe or a socket of another thread, which
then failed or read the wrong data.

Close the alert fd on thread exit only when msync is off. Without
WINEMSYNC nothing changes.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 #include "wine/server.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
 #include "unix_private.h"
+#include "msync.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(thread);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(seh);
@@ -1104,7 +1105,10 @@ static void contexts_from_server( CONTEXT *context, struct context_data server_c
  */
 static DECLSPEC_NORETURN void pthread_exit_wrapper( int status )
 {
-    close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->alert_fd );
+    /* Under msync the alert "fd" is the thread's index in the server's shared
+     * object table, not a descriptor; closing it would close whatever file
+     * the process has open under that number. */
+    if (!do_msync()) close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->alert_fd );
     close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->wait_fd[0] );
     close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->wait_fd[1] );
     close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->reply_fd );
